Instead of using manual bitwise operations and magic numbers like `31` and `5`, we can leverage the existing `ceil_div` utility defined in `flashinfer/utils.cuh`. This improves readability and maintainability while compiling to the same efficient instructions.

```
  // ceil(blockDim.x / 32): a trailing partial warp still contributes a value
  // to shared[] and must be included in the final reduction.
  bool is_mask = threadIdx.x < ceil_div(blockDim.x, 32U);
```

